<title>JAPAN: Japan Apr M2+CD money supply up 3.1 pct yr/yr - BOJ.</title>
<headline>Japan Apr M2+CD money supply up 3.1 pct yr/yr - BOJ.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's broadly defined money supply average of M2 plus certificates of deposit (CDs) grew a preliminary 3.1 percent in April from a year earlier, the Bank of Japan (BOJ) said on Friday.  </p>
<p>A breakdown of April money supply figures follows:</p>
<p>(Year-on-year percentage changes)</p>
<p>			    APR PRELIM  MAR REVISED</p>
<p>Unadjusted M2 + CDs     +3.1	 +2.8</p>
<p>   M1			 +9.0	 +9.3</p>
<p>   CDs		     +21.6	+12.6</p>
<p>Broadest Liquidity	+3.9	 +3.7</p>
<p>(Annualised month-on-month percentage changes)</p>
<p>			     APR PRELIM   MAR REVISED</p>
<p>Adjusted M2 + CDs	 +7.2	 +1.2</p>
<p>(Average outstanding yen levels)</p>
<p>			    APR PRELIM  MAR REVISED</p>
<p>Unadjusted M2+CDs    569.7 trln   563.7 trln</p>
<p>   M1		    179.0 trln   176.2 trln</p>
<p>   CDs		    24.0 trln    20.0 trln</p>
<p>			    APR PRELIM  MAR REVISED</p>
<p>Broadest liquidity 1,150.2 trln  1,140.9 trln</p>
<p>(NOTE: The broadest liquidity measure includes postal savings deposits at agricultural financial institutions and trust banks, bank debentures, Japanese government bonds, investment trusts and foreign bonds, along with M2 plus CDs.)</p>
</text>
